# Review package: ticket 03, c7036f6..54eebc2

## Commits
### 54eebc2
fix(state): batch mutating array methods on both kinds of state

Hookless state returned the native array methods raw, so a push woke
each subscriber once per property it wrote, while hooked state wrapped
them around the raw target and woke every subscriber on every call,
even one that changed nothing. Both kinds now read the same wrapper,
which applies the native method to its call receiver, the Proxy, inside
a batch. Every read and write passes the traps, so loop detection and
the state hooks observe them, equal values are skipped, and the batch
boundary wakes each subscriber at most once per call. The cache is
keyed by the native method because the wrapper no longer closes over a
target.

Tighten the sealed-array property test to assert the TypeError and a
working write afterwards, and pin the length notification on a direct
index write, which push no longer exercises unbatched.


